      <h1>Request data deletion</h1>
      <p>
        You can request deletion of your Lumière Archive (Hedonism Bot)
        information without logging in or having a Facebook account.
      </p>
      <ol>
        <li>
          Email <strong>[PRIVACY CONTACT EMAIL]</strong> with the subject
          “Lumière Archive data deletion”.
        </li>
        <li>
          Tell us which gallery or website your request concerns and the name or
          email associated with your account. If available, include your
          app-scoped Facebook user ID to help us locate it. Do not send your
          password or access token.
        </li>
        <li>
          Tell us whether you want your account and Facebook Login data deleted,
          particular photographs removed, facial analysis data deleted, or all
          personal information we hold about you deleted. For photographs,
          include the relevant album or image links and enough information to
          locate you.
        </li>
      </ol>
      <p>
        We may ask for limited additional information to verify the request and
        protect other people's information. We will acknowledge the request,
        explain any verification needed, and respond within the time required by
        applicable law.
      </p>
      <p>
        For a verified account deletion request, we delete the associated
        Facebook profile data, stored access tokens, and account information,
        and remove associated access permissions. Photo requests also cover
        related previews, captions, face crops, facial representations, and
        group associations to the extent they relate to the request. We will
        explain any information that cannot be deleted and why, including legal
        retention requirements. Backup copies expire under the backup lifecycle.
        Account deletion does not automatically identify every photograph in
        which you appear, so please provide image links when requesting photo
        removal.
      </p>
      <h2>Disconnect Facebook</h2>
      <p>
        You can also remove Lumière Archive from Facebook's
        <a href="https://www.facebook.com/settings?tab=applications"
          >Apps and Websites settings</a
        >. Disconnecting prevents further access through that authorization; use
        the email process above to delete information already held by the app.
        Signing out alone does not delete your account.
      </p>
